WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:01.290
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:08.620
A 2015 study ranked The United Kingdom as
the world leader in “soft power” – that’s

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.440
the ability to influence other nations by
“whispering in their ear”.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:18.190
The United States on the other hand is the
world leader in “hard power”, using their

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:21.360
vast military might to beat other countries
into submission.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:27.770
Put it this way, if the UK is Peter Baelish
then America is The Mountain.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:31.800
The difference in approaches between the two
nation’s foreign policies has a lot to do

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.880
with the way each country’s government functions.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.640
The British government has what’s called
a “division of power”, in which the Prime

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.750
Minister is not the country leader but is
simply the head of government as well as an

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:49.230
advisor to Her Majesty the Queen, whom is
the true head of state.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:55.130
The President of the United States however,
is the one and only head of state and executive

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:58.559
leader over the entire country and its people.

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:04.610
All this basically means that in the US, a
hell of a lot of power is given to one person.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:10.069
Apart from perhaps Putin, there are few heads
of state the have more individual power than

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.509
the US president.

00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:16.250
Even Kim Jong-Un has to share his power with
his deceased grandfather, who is technically

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.459
still President.

00:01:17.459 --> 00:01:22.549
But in reality, how real is the American President’s
power.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:25.479
How much power do they really possess?

00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:29.049
Will Donald Trump be able to build a wall
without permission from Congress?

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:31.049
Should you be scared?

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:37.130
The President of the United States or POTUS
is effectively a dictator.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:42.909
As long as he or she sticks within the confines
of the law, the POTUS is free to do whatever

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:43.939
they please.

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:50.030
However, if this power was pushed to its limits,
the POTUS would face impeachment, they would

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:53.140
have their presidency swiftly removed.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.270
So for this reason, and to gain the approval
of the general public, in the hopes of winning

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.659
a second term in four year’s time, presidents
often behave and do what the majority of the

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:05.249
American public wants them to do.

00:02:05.249 --> 00:02:12.209
But if a President weren’t sound of mind
and had no morals what could they theoretically

00:02:12.209 --> 00:02:13.799
do?

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:19.150
Well to start with an obvious one, the President
is “Commander in Chief” of the military

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:25.629
and can do whatever they please with it 1.5
million troops and endless toys.

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:32.579
And that’s not just the troops at home,
the President has total control of 800 military

00:02:32.579 --> 00:02:35.689
bases in 70 countries across the globe.

00:02:35.689 --> 00:02:41.620
Oh, and let’s not forget the 7,000 nuclear
warheads at the President’s disposal.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.409
What about a bit closer to home?

00:02:44.409 --> 00:02:48.640
What damage can the President do to their
own peoples.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:54.549
Since they are in charge of powerful organisations
such as the CIA, NSA and FBI, the President

00:02:54.549 --> 00:03:00.280
can find out whatever they like about pretty
much anyone and enforce any punishments they

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.420
so desire, in a heartbeat.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.030
The president also receives intelligence from
numerous allied countries.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:13.859
Lawmaking is a different kettle of fish and
is often where most presidents come unstuck

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.700
on their path to power.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:22.310
If the president wishes to amend or create
laws they have to create a bill which is passed

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:23.330
through congress.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:28.249
If it receives a majority vote in congress
the bill is passed to the president to sign,

00:03:28.249 --> 00:03:30.889
if he signs, it’s then the law.

00:03:30.889 --> 00:03:32.379
Simple, right?

00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:36.599
Well, that’s only if congress is on the
President’s side.

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:41.389
That’s to say the President’s political
party has more seats in congress than the

00:03:41.389 --> 00:03:43.030
opposition party.

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:47.209
Obviously, if you have more friends on your
side, then congress is more likely to vote

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:50.629
in favour of any bills you pass.

00:03:50.629 --> 00:03:55.959
And it just so happens that when Donald Trump
is inaugurated, he will have a majority number

00:03:55.959 --> 00:04:02.659
of Republican Seats, in both chambers of Congress:
The House of Representatives and the Senate.

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:08.939
In fact, the current Congress is the largest
Republican majority since the 1930s.

00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:14.779
Even if Trump’s majority congress doesn’t
vote in his favour of his fatuous plans, for

00:04:14.779 --> 00:04:22.001
some reason, he can always turn to an Executive
Order, which is basically there so the President

00:04:22.001 --> 00:04:27.580
can turn his middle finger up at Congress
and do what he likes anyway.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.050
Congress can always pass legislation that
opposes the President’s executive order,

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:38.180
but the President is free to veto anything
that Congress passes, so yeah, I think he

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:40.009
would probably do that.

00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:45.261
If a President’s executive order is in conflict
with the constitution it can be taken to the

00:04:45.261 --> 00:04:49.880
Supreme court, who have the power to either
allow it or quash it.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:53.789
Which historically would have acted as a nice
balance to stop the President’s power getting

00:04:53.789 --> 00:05:00.509
out of control – this next term however,
because some supreme justices are retiring

00:05:00.509 --> 00:05:06.169
soon, and other reasons, Donald Trump will
have the rare opportunity to pick who he would

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:12.099
like to be part of the Supreme Court, giving
him considerable leverage over the most powerful

00:05:12.099 --> 00:05:14.229
court in the land.

00:05:14.229 --> 00:05:17.889
He may get to replace four of the nine justices.

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:24.610
And when you consider that the average serving
time of a Supreme Court Justice is 26 years,

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:31.000
who he picks now will affect the country for
generations.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.940
Anyone who achieves the title of President
of the United States is inevitably going to

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:40.050
become one of the most powerful individuals
in the world.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:44.470
Franklin D. Roosevelt is often thought of
as the most powerful president in history.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:48.639
He certainly issued the most executive orders,
by a mile.

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:55.199
But with ever increasing usage of executive
orders and a Republican majority at his back,

00:05:55.199 --> 00:06:00.400
some experts theorise that Donald Trump will
have more power at his fingertips than any

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.590
predecessor.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:07.169
I’m sorry if you aren’t satisfied with
this answer, if so, you may want to look at

00:06:07.169 --> 00:06:12.740
emigrating to any of these five countries,
which statistically have the most stable political

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.389
systems in the world.

00:06:14.389 --> 00:06:28.789
I’d personally go for Denmark, they have
unbelievable breakfast pastries, but that’s

00:06:28.789 --> 00:06:35.979
just me.

00:06:35.979 --> 00:06:41.590
Thanks for watching.

